<title>USA: Continental buys office building in NC.</title>
<headline>Continental buys office building in NC.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Mortgage and Equity Trust said  Friday it had bought the Durham Center Office Building in Durham,  North Carolina, for of $21.1 million.</p>
<p>The Trust paid $6.3 million in cash, obtaining mortgage financing  for the remainder of the purchase price.</p>
<p>Durham Center is a 15-story Class &quot;A&quot; building that is currently 99  percent occupied. The property is in the downtown area of Durham,  which is one of the fastest growing areas in North Carolina, Continental  said.</p>
<p>Continental Mortgage and Equity Trust is a nationwide real estate  investment trust.</p>
</text>
